# Context-source ladder

**This is one of two files you author yourself** (the other is `CONCEPTS.md`).
Everything else in the support tree installs verbatim. Fill in the rows below with
your team's real sources, keep a compact copy of the table in the workspace root
`AGENTS.md`, and re-tune both together whenever a source class appears or retires.

The shape is deliberate: a **primary**, a **declared alternate**, and a **reserve
discipline**. Improvised fallbacks — broad catalog scans, neighboring checkouts,
unscoped searches — are what turn a cheap question into an expensive session, so
every branch names its approved alternate up front instead of dead-stopping and
letting the agent invent one.

## The ladder

Replace these rows. The first three are near-universal; the rest are examples of
the *shape* a row takes.

| Question class | Primary | Declared alternate |
|---|---|---|
| Repo purpose or layout (which repo, what is in it) | Repo digests (`context-fabric/records/generated/repo-digests/`) | Hydrated checkout under `${AGENTIC_REPO_CHECKOUT_ROOT}/` |
| Code-level detail (APIs, logic, config) | Hydrated checkout (hydrate via a reviewed sync manifest) | Digest for orientation + an explicit note that checkout inspection is needed |
| System / ownership fact (which system, who runs it, how systems relate) | Context Fabric records (`context-fabric/records/`) | Ask the named system steward |
| {{Governed domain fact — policy, standard, regulation}} | {{Your governed reference source; check its own status/freshness signal before relying}} | {{Web search, cited, with a note that the source lacked coverage}} |
| {{Product decision history or prior synthesis}} | {{The product area's `docs/` lanes}} | {{Ask the area steward}} |
| {{Live tickets / wiki pages}} | {{Your tracker, only when the doctor's capability report shows the credential loaded}} | {{Ask the user to fetch or paste; do not guess at ticket contents}} |
| External / current-events context | Web search with citations | — |

## Reserve discipline (token budget)

- Load the specific record, digest, or file section that answers the question —
  never a whole reference bundle, a full catalog, or an entire repository tree.
- Prefer generated summaries (digests, census records, status reports) over raw
  sources when the question is orientation-level; drop to raw sources only for
  detail the summary cannot carry.
- Inspect before reading in full: listings, manifests, and frontmatter first.
- A freshness-gated source past its `do_not_rely_after` date is treated as
  **unavailable**: use the declared alternate and say why.

## Maintenance

Add a row when a source class appears (the repo-digest row entered the day digests
shipped; an MCP-backed source would add its own). Update the compact copy in the
workspace root `AGENTS.md` in the same change — the two must not drift.
